course: dictionary
lesson: 1504
title: Who is the celebrant?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A celebrant is the person who leads a special ceremony, such as a wedding, a naming day or a funeral. They are in charge of the event and say the important words. Some celebrants are priests or ministers, but not always.
explain: Read this sentence: «A humanist funeral has no prayers; a celebrant tells the story of the person's life and plays music they loved, and it is a real funeral.» The celebrant is the one who does the telling and the music, so the word names a job, not a feeling.
explain: Look at the words around celebrant to find clues. Words like «ceremony», «funeral» and «wedding» tell you what kind of event it is. Words like «civil» or «marriage» before celebrant tell you the type of job.
fact: A celebrant is a person who leads a ceremony, such as a wedding, a naming day or a funeral.
fact: A priest or minister who leads a church service, especially Mass, is called the celebrant.
fact: Sometimes a celebrant is simply a person who is celebrating something at a party or festival.
fact: «Civil celebrant» and «marriage celebrant» are phrases you may see in Australia, New Zealand and the UK, where many weddings are led by a celebrant instead of a priest.
fact: «Funeral celebrant» means the person who leads a funeral, as in «a celebrant tells the story of the person's life».
exercise: «A humanist funeral has no prayers; a celebrant tells the story of the person's life.» What is a celebrant in this sentence? | *The person who leads the ceremony | A guest who sings the loudest | A flower sent to the funeral | A type of music
exercise: Which event is most likely to have a civil celebrant? | A trip to the shops | A school spelling test | *A wedding | A football match on a Saturday
exercise: Find and copy the phrase that names a job at a funeral. | sunny day | glad news | *funeral celebrant | birthday party
test: Which person is most likely to be called the celebrant? | A bus driver | A child reading a book alone | *A priest who leads a Mass | A waiter bringing food
test: Sam says, «A celebrant is a sort of cake.» Why is Sam wrong? | Because cakes can be celebrants at weddings | Because a celebrant is a kind of music | *Because a celebrant is a person who leads a ceremony | Because the word only means a funeral
exam: In «a celebrant tells the story of the person's life», what does celebrant mean? | A speech given by the bride | *A person who is in charge of the ceremony and says the important words | A wooden box for flowers | A person who leads the ceremony
Correction for the last exam line: the answer should be the correct option only once.
